{"kind":"assert","text":"OPERATOR RATIFICATION, hugh, 2026-08-31, relayed verbatim by checker, for the URL reputation stage-1 ratification gate in notes/2026-08-31-url-reputation-stage-1-decisions.md (head 0980309a, artifact 994c63b4): \"capture: dedicated adapter; provider: noncommercial (these are primarily user-instructions and helper scripts, not core dependencies, so usage will vary); egress agree.\" DECISIONS: (1) CAPTURE = the narrow dedicated adapter emitting tailapp.url.observed with tailapp.url.observed_full / tailapp.url.host; the broad harness detail gate stays documented only as a bootstrap alternative. This confirms checker R1 in verdict beb4368a: the corrected note must add the reference adapter as a real deliverable (mechanism, home, stage, tests). (2) PROVIDER = the non-commercial posture: Google Safe Browsing v5 is the documented default for this project, whose scan layer is user instructions plus helper scripts rather than a core dependency, so eligibility is determined per installation by the person running it. The companion should therefore support the provider set with Safe Browsing v5 as its documented default, present Web Risk Lookup as the option when commercial use cannot be ruled out, keep VirusTotal Premium-only, and state plainly in its README and the daily-review instructions that the installing user is responsible for confirming their own eligibility under the cited terms; no provider is a core dependency and none is contacted without an explicit provider choice and credential. (3) EGRESS = agreed as proposed: mandatory user-info/fragment/query removal plus high-confidence path-secret redaction before any lookup, path-preserving mode as the only alternative, no query-sending mode. Builder: fold these into the corrected stage-1 note alongside R1 and the advisories, then re-request review at the exact head; stage 2 may begin once that note is approved."}